{"c":[{"id":"0f5b9811057334dd","sum":"Reader AX lore: Chrome titles its top AXGroup/AXWebArea (keep out of keys), rejects AXManualAccessibility yet exposes web AX, posts no DOM-text notices (E1/E8); background AppKit fixtures need makeKey() for focus; caret-screen acts only in --act-pids, rechecks fail closed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b99fccd1ca3e2300","sum":"Chrome: top AXGroup is named after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title, so keep both out of element keys (E8); Chrome/Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) yet expose web AX, Electron accepts it; web pages post no AX notification for DOM text changes (E1).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-2317db88abe7ef57","text":"Chrome names its top AXGroup after the window title and AXWebArea after the page title; keep both out of element keys or every key moves on a title change (E8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T100848Z-7a26e801e62c7446","text":"Chrome and Helium reject AXManualAccessibility (-25205) but still expose web AX; Electron apps accept it. Web pages post no AX notification for DOM text, insert or remove changes (E1).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7284de3ea53779af","sum":"Fixtures and acting: a non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus only inside its key window (fixtures makeKey() before makeFirstResponder); caret-screen write/press act only in --act-pids, a subset of --only-pids, and rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T100848Z-bac1844f3b887c52","text":"A non-frontmost AppKit app posts AX focus notifications only inside its key window; fixtures call makeKey() (no activation) before makeFirstResponder.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T114801Z-32531afb7e4fe1e0","text":"caret-screen write/press verbs act only in --act-pids, which must be a subset of --only-pids; without it the reader only reads. Rechecks fail closed on unreadable role/subrole/value/label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfe456d6c1deaf07","sum":"Fill recency is the window before the form's last focus (the latest made Jev answer none); caret-fixture deactivates on becoming active, so poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs. RollingText.find credits the latest window: use findAll. Replay tests tick on a fixed 250 ms stream grid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"55197345bf228f3c","sum":"Fill recency takes the window before the form's last focus (the latest focus made Jev answer none); caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app held the foreground, so it now deactivates on becoming active; poll lsappinfo front in GUI runs.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T114801Z-431742a743596ba6","text":"Fill recency: take the just-left window from focus history (the window before the form's last focus), not the latest focus; latest-focus made Jev answer none on most fields once the user moved to another form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T130715Z-7922f91e68f9ff52","text":"caret-fixture spawned from the frontmost app (T3 or a terminal) became the active app and held the foreground for a whole run; it now deactivates on becoming active. Poll lsappinfo front during GUI runs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"478a07b8a88c6346","sum":"Pattern code: RollingText.find credits a value seen in two windows to the most recent one; use findAll and pick the window that explains every round. Replay tests tick the helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts, or dense streams delay every transfer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T143157Z-06f3c5b5c6254f49","text":"A value shown in two windows is credited by RollingText.find to the most recently seen one; pattern code must use findAll and pick the window that explains every round, or loop columns look like different sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T143157Z-9c4a82917dc22e00","text":"Replaying reader streams in tests: tick helper on a fixed 250 ms grid of stream time like main.ts; ticking only inside gaps >250 ms delays every transfer when messages are dense.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
